{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Your garment did not wear out from upon you</b>. The clouds of glory would smooth their clothing and press it like pressed garments, and likewise their little ones — as they grew, their clothing grew with them. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Deuteronomy 8:4) and the words of the Aggadah (Midrash Tehillim 23). But R. Abraham ibn Ezra wrote, and others said, that they brought out many garments, and it is possible that the nature of the manna does not produce perspiration, and likewise he said <b>and your foot did not swell</b>, that He gave them strength or led them slowly. But his words are not correct, for Moses mentions this to them to say that through the performance of the commandment they will have food and clothing and renewed strength, just as they lived on the manna for forty years and their garments endured and no ailment came to their feet — and all of it from the working of the miracle, for upon every utterance of the mouth of HaShem does man live and sustain himself. And if you were to cover a beam with a new garment for forty years, it would wear out even though there is no perspiration in it, all the more so a human who is a worm:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:46:48.209063709Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}